{
  "sticker": "leaf",
  "called": "the big leaf",
  "skeleton": "one giant round leaf on a thick stalk growing straight up out of the ground, like an umbrella: root at the stalk's foot in the ground; the foot (the curled new leaf and the little sheath leaves round the stalk's base) on root, in front of the stalk, so the stalk's turning foot is always hidden under it; stalk bone at the stalk's foot; blade bone at the top of the stalk where the leaf meets it (the leaf drawn in front of the stalk's top end); a drooping leaf and a furled young leaf swap in for the blade. A plant with no face: it only moves as wind, rain or a bump would move it.",
  "sheets": [
    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of one giant round leaf on a thick green stalk growing straight up out of the ground like an umbrella. Draw it as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate pieces laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every piece at the size it has in image 1 (if they do not all fit, draw them all a little smaller, at the same scale as each other).\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no piece touching or overlapping another:\n1. the big round leaf alone, without its stalk: glossy green with lighter veins and a gently wavy edge, exactly as in image 1, with the notch in its lower edge where the stalk meets it; the veins all start from the top of that notch.\n2. the stalk alone: the long, thick, smooth green stalk of image 1, from its foot to its top, drawn whole, including its foot that the little leaves hide and its top that the big leaf hides; its top end is a soft rounded end with no outline drawn across it.\n3. the stalk's foot alone: the little pointed sheath leaves wrapped round the bottom of the stalk and the short curl of new leaf beside them, exactly as at the bottom of image 1, without the stalk (where the stalk would rise out of them, their top is open).\n4. the same big leaf drooping, heavy with rain: its round edges hanging down all round like a half-closed umbrella, its middle still on top, the same green and veins, seen from the same side, a little narrower and taller than piece 1, without its stalk.\n5. the big leaf as a young leaf, not yet open: rolled up tight into a slim upright green scroll, like the curl at the stalk's foot, its veins showing, without its stalk.\n\nEvery piece is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another piece, with its edges clean and smooth. It is a plant, not a character: no face, no eyes, no mouth. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the pieces beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows, no ground, no grass, no rain, no drops. Fully transparent background."
    },
